### Problem:
You are tasked with implementing a simple observer pattern in a C# program. The observer pattern is a behavioral design pattern that defines a one-to-many dependency between objects so that when one object changes state, all its dependents are notified and updated automatically. In this problem, you will create a simplified implementation of the observer pattern using C#.

You are given a class `Column` which represents a column in a table. The `Column` class has a boolean property `isClicked` and a method `NotifyIsClickedChanged()` which notifies the observers when the `isClicked` property changes. Your task is to implement the observer pattern by creating a class `Observer` that subscribes to changes in the `isClicked` property of the `Column` class and performs an action when the property changes.

Your `Observer` class should have a method `Update(Column column)` which is called when the `isClicked` property of the `Column` changes. When the `isClicked` property becomes `true`, the `Update` method should print "Column is clicked". When the `isClicked` property becomes `false`, the `Update` method should print "Column is unclicked".

You need to implement the `Observer` class and demonstrate the observer pattern by creating an instance of the `Column` class, attaching an observer to it, and changing the `isClicked` property to see the observer in action.

